// The existential over labels, on a region it can use today.
//
// exists(l, labels, psi) holds where psi holds for some label l of the image
// labels. The variable becomes a parameter of every declaration beside the
// frame reference, and the exists unrolls into or(psi(1),...,psi(K)), K the
// bound given with --maxlabels, so that the reduction of the second pass shares
// whatever does not depend on l. The bound is a hypothesis: a label past it is
// a witness the disjunction misses. Naming the labelling is what makes it
// checkable -- the third pass prints max(labels) .<=. K beside the program --
// and computable beforehand, by the same specification under --probe.
//
// The labels come from the temporal footprint: lcc is computed once, on the
// union of the lesion over every frame, so the same label names the same
// component at every time. That needs the footprint to be taken at an absolute
// frame: under the diamond, until(tt,lesion) alone would be "eventually, from
// the next frame on", and its lcc a different labelling. initially(phi) is phi
// at frame 0 whatever temporal operators stand around it, so the third pass
// emits a single lcc, over lesion at every frame, and one eq per label.
//
// The formula reads "some footprint component is a lesion now and still is at
// the next frame": with a footprint that is the persistence per component that
// tracked will refine, and it is a program VoxLogicA 1 accepts as it stands.
let study = load("study.nii.gz")
let lesion = gt(intensity(frame(study,n)),500)
let footprint = initially(lcc(until(tt,lesion)))
let region(l) = and(eq(footprint,l),lesion)
save "persistent" exists(l,footprint,and(region(l),diamond(region(l))))
